      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T20:19:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do produce such an error, but only when parameter lists match; different return values and modifiers are allowed for different parameter sets.\n\n(Some functions like `mix` do need different modifiers on different parameter sets... some are `$es3` and others are not.)\n\nIn this scenario you would actually get `$foo` renamed across the board, because `minifyPrivateFunctionName` renames the entire overload chain as soon as it finds a private non-exported function. You need to flag every overload with `$export` or exporting won\u0027t work. Not ideal but it\u0027s not _that_ bad?",
      "parentUuid": "c76bf599_63975b2d",
      "revId": "73d5d92d5d4bf3fb368e5f37f559ef44e0b99c59",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
